<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

    <!--
    CRT.UI - Avalonia controls shared by CRT's Drafts tab and its Maintainer tab. They were two
    applications (CRT.App and the separate CRT Maintainer) until 2026-09-29, when the maintainer
    application became CRT's Maintainer tab; the library stays, because the sharing is still real
    and CRT.Data's rules are painted here, not in either tab.

    It exists for the TABLE EDITOR (owner request, 2026-09-25): the Drafts tab's "Edit in table
    format" and the Maintainer tab's table are the same control, so a fix or a colour change
    reaches both. Its rules are in CRT.Data (BoardTableDocument and friends); this library only
    paints them.

    Rules for what may live here: a control BOTH tabs show, which touches nothing of CRT's own
    orchestration (no Main, no DataManager, no UserSettings, no Logger - CRT.Data's CrtLog is the
    logging seam). Anything that needs one of those stays in CRT.App.

    Dragging/ holds the other shared piece (2026-09-27): ListRowDrag, the drag-a-row-with-a-dashed-
    placeholder handling of the Drafts tab's schematic images, which the Maintainer tab's
    drop-down placement uses too, and RowDragSlots, its maths (the worklog editor's lists use that).

    Its colours are its own (BoardTable/BoardTableColors.axaml), merged by CRT's App.axaml; the few
    general theme keys it borrows (Bg, Table_Bg, the Cancel button's colours, Text_Fail_Fg) CRT
    defines itself.
    -->
    <PropertyGroup>
        <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
        <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
        <AvaloniaUseCompiledBindingsByDefault>true</AvaloniaUseCompiledBindingsByDefault>
        <TreatWarningsAsErrors Condition="'$(Configuration)' == 'Release'">true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    </PropertyGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <PackageReference Include="Avalonia" Version="12.1.3" />
        <PackageReference Include="ProDataGrid" Version="12.1.0.4" />
    </ItemGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <ProjectReference Include="..\CRT.Data\CRT.Data.csproj" />
    </ItemGroup>

    <!--
    The applications reach the editor's internal members (the Drafts tab asks whether the draft is
    held open elsewhere, for instance), and the test projects reach its ...ForTests seams, exactly as
    they did while it lived in CRT.App.
    -->
    <ItemGroup>
        <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Classic-Repair-Toolbox" />
        <InternalsVisibleTo Include="CRT.App.Tests" />
    </ItemGroup>

</Project>
